course: dictionary
lesson: 15465
title: Meet the stomatopod
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A stomatopod is a sea animal that is also called a mantis shrimp. It has shrimp in its name, but it is not really a shrimp. It is related to crabs and shrimps, so it belongs to the same family of animals called crustaceans.
explain: «The stomatopod struck the snail shell with its front claws.» The clues are struck and claws. A stomatopod hits its food fast, like a punch. Try your meaning in the sentence: «The mantis shrimp struck the snail shell» still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Stomatopod is a scientific name for the whole group of these animals. Scientists use it when they talk about all of them, not just one kind. When you see the word in science, ask yourself: is this one animal, or the whole group?
fact: A stomatopod is a mantis shrimp, a sea animal related to crabs and shrimps.
fact: Stomatopods are crustaceans, which means they have a hard outer shell.
fact: Stomatopods hunt by striking their prey with super-fast front claws.
fact: Their punch is one of the fastest movements of any animal, and it can crack shells and even aquarium glass.
fact: They live in warm shallow seas, often in burrows, and their eyes can see colours that humans cannot.
exercise: «The stomatopod sped out of its burrow to catch a crab.» What is a stomatopod? | A kind of rock found on beaches | *A mantis shrimp, a sea animal | A fish with no fins | A tiny bird that lives in trees
exercise: Scientists say a stomatopod's punch is one of the fastest movements of any animal. What does fastest mean? | Slowest | Loudest | *Quickest | Heaviest
exercise: Which word is the scientific name for the whole group of these sea animals? | Burrow | Claw | Sea | *Stomatopod
test: «The stomatopod cracked the crab shell with one quick strike.» What does the word stomatopod mean? | *A mantis shrimp, a sea animal with super-fast front claws | A bird of warm seas | A large bird's nest | A crab with eight legs
test: In science lessons, what are stomatopods famous for? | Singing loudly at night | *Their super-fast punch and their amazing eyes | Flying high over mountains | Eating plants in the forest
exam: «The stomatopod lives in a burrow in a warm shallow sea.» Which sentence about stomatopods is true? | They are a kind of plant that grows on rocks | *They live in warm shallow seas, often in burrows | They live in cold, deep ice | They cannot move their front claws
